ID: Ch4-Intro
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_bloodied == 0 && v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 0) {

Daren paces outside our cave, broad shoulders rigid beneath his plate armor. The moment we come within earshot, his voice cuts across the clearing—not quite lecturing, but making it abundantly clear he expected us back an hour ago.

Kate brushes past him with a dismissive flick of her wrist, mumbling that the morning's nuisance exhausted her, and slips into the cool shade of the cave to sleep. As she passes my shoulder, her gaze catches mine for a fraction of a second—no nod, no words, but none of yesterday's iron either. Just the flat acknowledgment of someone who held the other flank. Then she is past, and the moment dissolves into the cave's dark. Daren turns to me, brow furrowed, and I give him the short version—the Duke of Bagelberry and his crossbow ambush.

"You're fortunate to have walked out of there in one piece," Daren grumbles, rubbing the bridge of his nose. "Why bother with a strategy council yesterday if everyone scatters the moment the sun comes up?"

Once his temper settles, the two of us take up positions at the mouth of the cave, scanning the tree line.

Standing watch in the quiet, our talk turns back to the tournament and the utter lack of order we've seen so far.

"I can't make sense of it," Daren says, pacing a tight line over the gravel. "What are the organizers thinking? Admitting commoners without a drop of magic into the contest, letting contestants slaughter one another before the objectives are even proclaimed... It's as though human lives are completely disposable to them."

"Because to them, they are," I say. "Think back to the entry pact. The victor is bound by oath to defend Varathia in the event of an overseas invasion. People signed without a second thought because no one has dared invade this continent in millennia, but that's the angle. They don't care about a fair tournament. They want the strongest living weapon on the planet stationed on their borders as a scarecrow. The dead along the way are just chaff."

"Even so," Daren says, frowning out toward the canopy, "if their sole purpose is securing a champion, why the delay? Every passing hour wastes energy and lives. Wouldn't they want the contest settled as swiftly as possible?"

}
#if(v_ch3_bloodied == 1 && v_ch3_kate_badly_hurt == 0) {

