ID: Ch4-Defeat
TEXT:

#if(v_ch3_tactics != 2) {
"I'd rather face Dave directly than play decoy," I say. "Ending this swiftly is safer than stretching it out until you can reinforce me."

"As you wish. What is the plan?"

"Watch."

}
#if(v_ch3_tactics == 2) {
"I've been waiting for this," I say, fixing my eyes on Cutthroat Dave.

"What is the plan?"

"Watch."

}
choice("Continue", Ch4-Defeat2, v_current_scene = Ch4-Defeat2)


ID: Ch4-Defeat2
TEXT:

set(v_ch4_dave_defeat,1) if (v_strength == 3)
set(v_ch4_dave_defeat,2) if (v_agility == 3 && v_strength < 3)
set(v_ch4_dave_defeat,3) if (v_reflexes == 3 && v_agility < 3 && v_strength < 3)
set(v_ch4_dave_defeat,0) if (v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_agility == 3 && v_strength < 3 || v_reflexes == 3 && v_agility < 3 && v_strength < 3 || v_strength == 3)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)
#if(v_strength == 3) {

I scoop a jagged granite boulder from the dirt—easily fifty pounds—and whip it straight at Cutthroat Dave's chest with the full pneumatic recoil of tier-three strength.

The cutthroat attempts to interpose two of his hovering daggers, but the mass crushes through the enchantments like paper. The boulder slams squarely into his sternum with a sickening crunch of shattered ribs, lifting him off his boots and pinning him violently against the trunk of a pine. He slides down into the needles, gasping on bloody foam, hands clawing weakly at the dirt.

One more strike will finish him.

}
#if(v_agility == 3 && v_strength < 3) {

I snatch a heavy stone from the loam and hurl it at Cutthroat Dave to force his guard.

The cutthroat intercepts it with two hovering daggers, steel sparking against stone.

"This ain't no rock-throwing contest, boy! You'd better be ready for what's coming!"

"I have his focus," I tell Daren. "Go!"

Daren breaks into a charge, shield up, bearing down on Dave's mercenaries before they can form ranks.

The remaining flying knives whip through the air in a converging spread. With tier-three agility humming through my legs, the world seems to drag. I pivot inside the arc of the first two blades, duck the third, and close the distance before Dave can reset his stance.

I cross the gap in two strides, dagger driving in for his throat. He parries with the pair of knives gripped in his fists, the impact jolting up his forearms, eyes blowing wide as he registers my speed.

"I don't know what kind of spell you're running, boy, but you can't outrun steel!"

Three tethered daggers wheel around to strike my back. I drop my center of gravity, spinning clear as the blades shear air where my neck was a heartbeat ago. We're in an open clearing; I know their turn radius and terminal velocity.

I weave a spiraling perimeter around him, cutting sharp angles across the moss to fracture his tracking. He pivots wildly to keep his front facing me, but his boots slip on loose gravel, his balance tearing at the seams. Every time his eyes drift, I feint inside his reach, forcing frantic parries that leave his guard ragged.

There. A stumble on an exposed root—his line of sight breaks for half a second.

I drive forward off my back foot, accelerating through his blind spot. He tries to cross his daggers in desperate defense, but my blade slides beneath his guard and punches deep into his right side, missing the heart but tearing clean through muscle and fat.

One more clean strike will end this.

}
#if(v_reflexes == 3 && v_agility < 3 && v_strength < 3) {

I scoop a stone from the dirt and whip it across the clearing.

Dave knocks it aside with a pair of orbiting daggers, sneering.

"This ain't no rock-throwing contest, boy! You'd better be ready for what's coming!"

"He's locked on me," I call to Daren. "Clear the flanks!"

Daren charges Dave's henchmen with a roar, drawing their front line away.

Four enchanted daggers streak toward my chest in a tight diamond formation. I lack the raw foot speed to outrun them, but tier-three reflexes make their approach appear deliberate, almost mechanical. I read the trajectory of the lead blade, slip sideways by three inches, and let the edge whisper past my tunic.

Two more daggers whip in from the flank, boxing me out. Every advance is blocked by a hovering wall of steel.

"My daggers have a mind of their own, stillwater!" Dave barks, grinning through yellow teeth. "You'll never break past them!"

A mind of their own. The enchantment runs on an automated proximity loop—he isn't actively piloting each vector. It's a tracking routine, which means it follows simple geometric intercepts.

I deliberately bait three of the hovering knives into trailing my sprint, then charge straight at Cutthroat Dave. As expected, two guard-blades snap into position in front of his chest to intercept me. At the last possible fraction of a second, I drop flat and slide across the pine needles beneath the guard-blades, kicking back to my feet on Dave's right flank.

Dave braces to parry with the knives in his hands, completely blind to the three tracking daggers chasing my slipstream from behind. Before he can recalibrate his tether, two of his own enchanted blades punch through his abdomen, and a third bites deep into his thigh.

He drops to one knee with a strangled cry, blood pooling around his boots.

One more blow will finish him.

}
#if(v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3) {

I grab a rock and fling it at Dave with everything I have.

He bats it out of the air with two hovering daggers, laughing with cruel ease.

"This ain't no rock-throwing contest, boy! You'd better be ready for what's coming!"

"I have him!" I yell to Daren. "Take the others!"

Daren rushes the henchmen, but the cutthroat's daggers are already closing the distance at blinding speed.

Four blades converge on my position. I manage to twist away from the first two, but the third and fourth bury themselves deep into my left thigh and calf. A searing jolt of agony rips through my leg, and I collapse into the dirt, clutching the wounds as crimson stains the moss.

Cutthroat Dave saunters toward me, his remaining daggers fanning out into a lethal ring around my skull, points gleaming six inches from my throat.

"It's over, boy. Too late to beg now. My blades like to take their time carving up fresh meat. Say your prayers, you arrogant little—"

Six blades in play. Two in my flesh, two hovering, two in his fists—and an empty bandolier.

Enchanted steel needs a tether, and an automated proximity loop only tracks vectors, not intent. Bleeding out on the moss, I force a choked laugh and expose my neck, baiting his strike.

Dave sneers and lunges, driving his right-hand blade down in a furious killing thrust.

At the final fraction of an inch, I jerk my shoulder sideways. The descending dagger grazes my collarbone and plunges into the loam, right through the tracking arc of the two hovering guard-blades. The tethers intersect. The proximity loop short-circuits in a violent screech of overloaded mana, and the magnetic feedback snaps inward with catastrophic force.

Both airborne daggers violently reverse direction, converging directly on the master tether. Before Dave can pull his hands back, his own enchanted steel drives through his chest and sternum, followed instantly by the second pair tearing into his ribs.

Dave gasps, his eyes bulging in choked shock. He collapses face-first into the needles, his own daggers pinning him to the dirt, dead before his forehead hits the loam.

I lie on my back in the dirt, clutching my bleeding thigh, breath sawing raggedly through my teeth. My hands won't stop shaking. I didn't win this fight. I barely tripped an exploit before bleeding out.

From the shadow of a weeping pine at the treeline, a soft voice drifts over the clearing.

"Do not make a habit of that, courier."

Eiden stands leaning against the bark, hands in his pockets, placid, closed-eyed smile unchanged. He hasn't moved an inch.

"You!" Daren's roar echoes across the clearing as he cuts down the last mercenary and sprints toward the stillwater with broadsword raised.

With a lazy flick of two fingers, Eiden triggers a sleep ward. Daren's eyes glaze instantly, his boots tangling in mid-stride, and he crashes face-first into the loam, sliding several feet in his heavy plate before coming to a dead stop.

"Truly, this is becoming repetitive," Eiden sighs.

He turns his head toward me, the empty smile lingering.

"Tell me, Barry... what sort of courier gets butchered before he even steps out of the waystation? I have half a mind to demand my coin back for your services."

"I... I'll make sure the message arrives."

"That's the spirit," he murmurs, his form already shimmering like heat off summer stone.

As his outline dissolves into the trees, his voice carries back on the wind, soft and chillingly clear:

"Deliver my words, Barry. Do not fail me again."

}
choice("Attempt to kill him", Ch4-Defeat-kill, v_current_scene = Ch4-Defeat-kill) if (v_strength == 3)
choice("Attempt to knock him out", Ch4-Defeat-spare, v_current_scene = Ch4-Defeat-spare) if (v_strength == 3)
choice("Aim for the kill", Ch4-Defeat-kill, v_current_scene = Ch4-Defeat-kill) if (v_agility == 3 && v_strength < 3 || v_reflexes == 3 && v_agility < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Aim to neutralize him, but don't kill him", Ch4-Defeat-spare, v_current_scene = Ch4-Defeat-spare) if (v_agility == 3 && v_strength < 3 || v_reflexes == 3 && v_agility < 3 && v_strength < 3)
choice("Next chapter", Ch5-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = Ch5-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, v_ch4_ending = 6, special:checkpoint_save) if (v_agility < 3 && v_reflexes < 3 && v_strength < 3)


ID: Ch4-Defeat-kill
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch4_cutthroat,1)
achievement("Defeated Cutthroat Dave",v_ac_ch4_cutthroat)
#if(v_ch4_dave_defeat == 1) {
I scoop another heavy stone from the earth and put the full recoil of tier-three strength into one final throw. Dave tries to interpose his remaining blades, but his reaction is half a second too slow; the rock takes him squarely in the temple. His body goes limp before it hits the moss, the floating daggers clattering lifeless to the ground.

The surviving mercenaries freeze in horror.

"Gods above, Barry!" Daren calls over the din. "You don't pull a punch, do you?"

"I'm not finished."

I snatch two more jagged stones from the dirt and whip them across the clearing. Both hit with sickening cracks, dropping two of the mercenaries in their tracks.

The remaining thugs break into panicked shrieks and bolt blindly for the timber. I sling one more stone in their general direction, but let them run. Chasing through dense brush would be useless, and with the terror written across their faces, they won't be coming back.

From the shadows of the tree line comes the slow, rhythmic sound of clapping hands. Eiden leans casually against a birch, hands in his pockets, that placid, closed-eyed smile across his face.

"Impressive, Barry," he says mildly. "One rarely sees stat boosters deployed with such ruthless economy."

"You!" Daren roars, turning and sprinting toward the stillwater with broadsword drawn.

With a lazy flick of two fingers, Eiden triggers a sleep ward. Daren's eyes glaze instantly, his boots tangling in mid-stride, and he crashes into the loam, sliding several feet in his heavy plate before coming to a dead stop.

"Seriously, this is becoming a habit," Eiden murmurs.

"You understand how these devices work too?" I ask, catching my breath.

"I do. And more importantly, I understand why that particular device functions so exceptionally well for you. Have you ever wondered why that is, Barry?"

He is right. The stat booster has exceeded every mathematical ceiling I calculated before sailing. I assumed my models were flawed, but the energetic efficiency is impossible for an ordinary human aura.

"I have. But I don't suppose you plan on explaining it."

"Of course not. Where is the entertainment in giving away the ending? But don't despair—stay alive on this continent, and your answers will find you."

His smile sharpens.

"Deliver my message, Barry. Do not fail me."

He turns and melts into the shadowed pines, leaving nothing but the rustle of wind through needles.

}
#if(v_ch4_dave_defeat == 2) {
I step inside his ragged guard and drive my blade clean between his ribs. His frame stiffens, a harsh gasp tearing from his throat, and as I wrench the steel free, his hovering daggers lose their enchantment and drop into the dirt. He collapses face-first into the needles.

Across the clearing, Daren has dismantled the mercenary line. Four bodies lie motionless; the rest have fled.

From the edge of the clearing comes the slow, rhythmic sound of clapping. Eiden leans against a pine, hands tucked into his loose trousers, his placid smile unchanged.

"Impressive, Barry. One rarely sees stat boosters deployed with such lethal efficiency."

"You!" Daren shouts, wheeling toward him with sword raised.

Eiden flicks two fingers. Daren drops in mid-stride, his armor clattering against the rock as sleep takes him instantly.

"Truly, this is getting ridiculous," Eiden sighs.

"You know how stat boosters operate?" I ask, wiping my blade.

"I do. And I know precisely why that instrument yields such extraordinary returns in your hands. Have you never questioned that, Barry?"

The thought has haunted me since yesterday. The power transfer rates defy standard arcane theory.

"I have. But I doubt you intend to satisfy my curiosity."

"Naturally not. The mystery is half the journey. Survive this tournament, and the truth will catch up with you."

He turns toward the dense woods.

"Deliver my words, Barry. Do not fail me."

With that, he dissolves into the gloom of the forest.

}
#if(v_ch4_dave_defeat == 3) {
I lunge forward, driving my dagger home beneath his breastbone. His body spasms, hands clawing at my forearm, and then goes slack as life leaves him. His tethered knives tumble into the moss.

Across the clearing, Daren stands amidst the fallen mercenaries, lowering his broadsword.

From the trees comes the dry, measured sound of slow applause. Eiden steps from behind a trunk, smiling mildly with his eyes shut.

"Impressive work, Barry. Stat boosters are rarely handled with such tactical precision."

"You!" Daren yells, charging the stillwater.

Eiden raises two fingers. Daren's momentum cuts out as sleep overwhelms him, his armored frame sliding across the grass.

"This is becoming tedious," Eiden murmurs.

"You know the internal mechanics of these devices?" I ask.

"Inside and out. Including why your particular constitution extracts such staggering output from it. Have you never wondered about your own nature, Barry?"

The efficiency ratio has bothered me from the moment I calibrated the device on the ship.

"I have. Though I don't expect you to hand me the explanation."

"Perceptive. Why ruin the drama? Keep breathing on this continent, and you will learn everything in time."

He turns his back.

"Deliver my message, Barry. Do not fail me."

He vanishes into the deep green shadows.

}
choice("Next chapter", Ch5-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = Ch5-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, v_ch4_ending = 5, v_ch4_spared_dave = 0, special:checkpoint_save)


ID: Ch4-Defeat-spare
TEXT:

set(v_ac_ch4_cutthroat,1)
achievement("Defeated Cutthroat Dave",v_ac_ch4_cutthroat)
#if(v_ch4_dave_defeat == 1) {
I scoop another stone from the dirt, but pull the force of the throw, aiming to fracture his guard rather than his skull. With the reduced velocity, Dave manages to bat the projectile aside with two battered daggers.

He hacks up a glob of dark blood, coughing violently against the loam.

"You got lucky, stillwater! Caught me off balance! It won't happen twice!"

With a trembling hand, Dave rips a parchment scroll from inside his vest and crushes the wax seal. Azure arcane light spirals around his frame, and he vanishes on the spot—a high-tier emergency teleportation scroll.

Where does a cutthroat operating out of border ravines get his hands on instantaneous teleportation? A single parchment costs a merchant's ransom.

"Gods above, Barry!" Daren calls out. "You don't pull a punch, do you?"

"I actually did. And it let him slip away. But we're not finished."

I scoop a handful of coarse gravel from the loam and whip it across the clearing with tier-three strength. The stones hit Dave's mercenaries like canister shot, splintering leather and dropping three of them to their knees howling in pain.

"Did you see that?!" one of them screeches. "He threw gravel like ballista shot!"

"The boss broke! Fall back!"

The thugs scatter into the trees, tripping over roots in their haste. I don't bother pursuing; they are broken, terrified, and far from dangerous.

From the edge of the clearing comes the quiet, rhythmic sound of clapping. Eiden leans against a pine, hands in his pockets, smiling placidly.

"Impressive, Barry. One rarely sees stat boosters deployed with such restraint."

"You!" Daren bellows, charging the stillwater with his broadsword raised.

Eiden flicks two fingers. Daren drops in mid-stride, skidding through the pine needles as sleep overtakes him.

"Truly, this is becoming repetitive," Eiden sighs.

"You understand how these devices work?" I ask.

"I do. And I know why that stat booster functions so remarkably well for you in particular. Have you never wondered why that is, Barry?"

"I have. But I doubt you're going to hand over the answer."

"Of course not. Where would the entertainment be? Survive this continent, and the truth will find you."

He turns into the shadows.

"Deliver my message, Barry. Do not fail me."

He melts into the dark forest.

}
#if(v_ch4_dave_defeat == 2) {
I drive my dagger into his shoulder, pinning his arm, and slam my boot into his chest to force him down. Dave hits the loam, spitting blood, and frantically tears open a teleportation scroll from his tunic. Blue light flares, and he vanishes into thin air.

A teleportation scroll. Even second-rate smugglers rarely possess the coin for instantaneous transit.

Across the clearing, Daren stands among the defeated thugs, sword resting at his side.

From the trees comes the slow, measured applause of a spectator. Eiden steps into the light, smiling mildly with his eyes closed.

"Impressive, Barry. Ruthless and efficient."

"You!" Daren roars, lunging toward the stillwater.

Eiden raises two fingers; Daren's eyes shut and he crashes into the grass in a heap of plate armor.

"This is becoming tedious," Eiden murmurs.

"You know how stat boosters operate?" I ask.

"Better than most. And I know why your device produces such extraordinary results. Have you never wondered about that, Barry?"

"Every day. But you won't tell me."

"Naturally not. Why spoil the discovery? Keep yourself alive, and all will become clear."

He turns away.

"Deliver my message, Barry. Do not fail me."

He dissolves into the shadows.

}
#if(v_ch4_dave_defeat == 3) {
I drive the pommel of my dagger into Dave's jaw and follow with a sweeping kick that drops him flat. Before I can pin his wrists, he scrambles backward, crushing a parchment scroll against his chest. Azure runes ignite, whisking him away before my blade can bite.

Teleportation magic. Someone with serious backing gave him that fail-safe.

Across the clearing, Daren wipes his blade, having routed the remaining mercenaries.

From the woodline comes the sound of slow, solitary clapping. Eiden steps into view, hands in his pockets, smiling serenely.

"Impressive work, Barry. You adapt quickly."

"You!" Daren shouts, rushing the stillwater.

With a flick of his wrist, Eiden drops Daren into a dead sleep before he can cross three strides.

"A predictable reaction," Eiden sighs.

"You understand the engineering behind stat boosters?" I ask.

"I do. And I understand why your device draws so much raw output from your body. Have you never questioned your own nature, Barry?"

"I have. But I know better than to expect charity from you."

"Good boy. Survive this tournament, and the answers will come."

He turns into the woods.

"Deliver my message, Barry. Do not fail me."

He vanishes into the gloom.

}
choice("Next chapter", Ch5-Intro, v_next_chapter_crash = 1, v_current_scene = Ch5-Intro, v_chapter_save_counter = 5, v_checkpoint_rich = 1, v_ch4_spared_dave = 1, v_ch4_ending = 5, special:checkpoint_save)
